  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
